From: LFRon <ronforever@outlook.com>
Date: 2026-08-15 20:55:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tu/kgsl: materialize fences for no-op submits

A Vulkan sync-fd payload may use fd -1 to represent an already-signaled
fence, but Android EGL native-fence consumers require a real sync_file. A
KGSL no-op queue submission whose waits were already satisfied could export
VK_SUCCESS with fd -1, leaving GLConsumer release synchronization on a stale
or black frame.

Represent the pure signaled result of a no-op submission as timestamp zero
on the submitting context, which is already retired, so the timestamp event
ioctl can create a valid immediately-signaled sync_file. Real external and
cross-queue dependencies are preserved.

Signed-off-by: LFRon <ronforever@outlook.com>
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
index 2e14201..3db801b 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
@@ -1557,6 +1557,12 @@ kgsl_queue_submit(struct tu_queue *queue, void *_submit,
                                    "refusing to submit an unsignaled semaphore wait to KGSL");
       }
 
+      if (wait_sync.state == KGSL_SYNCOBJ_STATE_SIGNALED) {
+         wait_sync.state = KGSL_SYNCOBJ_STATE_TS;
+         wait_sync.queue = queue;
+         wait_sync.timestamp = 0;
+      }
+
       if (signal_count == 1) {
          /* Move instead of duplicating the syncobj, as we don't need to
           * keep the original one around.
